      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When an onion is sliced, the cell walls are damaged, releasing enzymes called alliinases. These enzymes catalyze the reaction between alliin (a sulfur-containing compound) and water to produce allicin. Allicin then reacts with oxygen to form propanethial S-oxide, a gas that is released rapidly and responsible for the eye irritation and tear production.",
